{
	"_comment": "Typing vectors of Neo 2's own levels in the layout source emulation (docs/design/layout-source-format.md, « Emulation of what no .keylayout holds »). Each case replays steps on a fresh session of neo2_emulation.json, the table the source compiler writes for neo2_source.toml per platform, as emulation_vectors.json does; a case naming platforms is replayed on those only. Mod3 is held on Caps Lock (not on macOS, which never reports Caps Lock held) and on the ISO key left of Enter, Mod4 on the key right of left Shift and on AltGr, whose own AltGr the engine ignores while it holds Mod4. The base and Shift levels are native: a key the engine leaves alone types as the .keylayout does. The web emulation (source_emulation.js), the Lua engine of macOS and Linux (layouts/engine/composer/source_emulation.lua) and the AutoHotkey engine of Windows (modules/keymap/keylayout/source_emulation.ahk) replay them.",
